/*******************************************************************
 * File:        assemble_x86_64
 * Purpose:     Assembler backend for x86-64. Ported from Richard
 *              Russell's BBC BASIC assembler at
 *              riscos64-rtrussell-bbcbasic/src/bbasmb_x86_64.c
 *              (Copyright (c) 2021 R.T.Russell, used here under the
 *              same terms as the rest of this project). The
 *              instruction/operand/mnemonic data tables below are
 *              carried over unchanged from that source, since they
 *              are the exact list of instructions this backend
 *              supports and instructions[] must stay in this sorted
 *              order for the binary search in find_instruction() to
 *              work. Everything below that point has been rewritten
 *              against this library's line-at-a-time calling
 *              convention (assemble_context_t, callbacks, error
 *              blocks) in place of BASIC's global line cursor,
 *              expr()/expri(), poke() and error().
 *
 *              A deliberately limited x86-64 subset, matching the
 *              original: no privileged instructions, no
 *              SSSE3/SSE4/AVX. One further omission versus the
 *              original: MOV reg64,name resolving a BASIC/OS routine
 *              name to its address relies on a live runtime function
 *              registry this library has no equivalent of, so that
 *              specific form raises
 *              ASSEMBLE_X86_64_ERR_SYSTEM_CALL_UNSUPPORTED rather
 *              than resolving the name (embedding a string's bytes
 *              as immediate data, which does not need a runtime
 *              registry, is still supported).
 * Author:      Charles Ferguson (Gerph), after R.T.Russell
 ******************************************************************/

